<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Lipany</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1434</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hussite-wars">Hussite Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Lipany was fought east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a> on 30 May 1434 near the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hussite-wars">Hussite Wars</a>. An alliance of moderate Utraquists and Catholics defeated the radical Taborite and Orphan field armies, and their leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prokop-the-great">Prokop the Great</a> was killed. The battle ended radical Hussite power and opened the way to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/compacts-of-basel">Compacts of Basel</a> and the recognition of Sigismund as king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-lipany.jpg" alt="Battle of Lipany" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Luděk Marold · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Skupina_bratrsk%C3%BDch_vojev%C5%AFdc%C5%AF.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
